mphasizes the importance of proper nutrition for children, pregnant women, and lactating mothers, advocating for a varied diet that meets all necessary nutrient requirements. The organization also offers formulas for estimating energy expenditure and dietary needs, which are essential for understanding the nutritional status of different populations.\n\nIn addition to its focus on nutrition, the OMS addresses broader health topics such as active aging, telemedicine, and the use of information and communication technologies in healthcare. It provides guidelines for rehydration solutions and has developed international reference patterns for child growth, contributing to global health initiatives aimed at improving the quality of life.\n\nThe OMS is recognized for its leadership in global health matters, shaping the health research agenda, and providing critical data on health issues such as diabetes prevalence and obesity management. Through its extensive guidelines and recommendations, the OMS aims to optimize health opportunities and enhance the overall well-being of populations worldwide.\",69\r\n942,FIGURA 8,\"FIGURA 8 is a multifaceted entity that encompasses both culinary and scientific aspects. It features an illustration that showcases vegetables cooked to an al dente texture, which serves as a demonstration of the proper cooking technique for dysphagia diets, ensuring that individuals with swallowing difficulties can enjoy nutritious meals safely. Additionally, FIGURA 8 includes the World Health Organization's equations for estimating energy expenditure, providing a scientific framework for understanding energy needs. This combination of culinary guidance and health-related equations highlights FIGURA 8's role in promoting both dietary health and nutritional awareness.\",2\r\n1306,BRASIL,Brasil es un país que proporciona datos sobre el crecimiento infantil y la nutrición en el contexto de la Organización Mundial de la Salud (OMS).,2\r\n7870,MUJERES EMBARAZAD